                        "entry_id": "22e4a2b0-cde0-3bbc-89d5-a81d7ae0127f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A canary that is of a single color with no dark feathers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b4b695b-fa61-400d-95f2-ec807b0cec3e",
                                "sense_id": "8ab6ed99-3690-3742-9ae6-10efeae4ed23",
                                "text": "I know not, indeed, if the artist could give the beautiful orange which distinguish ^([sic]) the jonque, or the mellowness of tint that pervades the mealy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "369cfbdc-0fe7-4ec1-a326-2be4adb4b95e",
                                "sense_id": "8ab6ed99-3690-3742-9ae6-10efeae4ed23",
                                "text": "Canary-birds, however, are not likely to become extinct; […] each flock is said to have its own peculiar song, but we must not think the \"jonques,\" so popular among us, form the majority in a flock."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e80a9683-90d4-4153-becc-385f2df7de28",
                                "sense_id": "8ab6ed99-3690-3742-9ae6-10efeae4ed23",
                                "text": "Pied birds are produced by matching a green jonque with a clean jonque, or a mealy hen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
